---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro"
---
<Page title="How it works">
	<section class="intro">
		<p class="eyebrow">One value, two beginnings</p>
		<h1>One database. Two ways to read it.</h1>
		<p>
			Astro waits for the atom defaults, renders the draft cards with SPA, and
			places the results in a JSON sidecar. The browser consumes those values
			before hydrating the existing cards.
		</p>
		<p>
			A reset calls the default again. Its server value has already been
			consumed, so the client closure calls tRPC for a fresh database read.
			Editing or resetting one workspace leaves the other alone.
		</p>
		<p>
			Navigation disposes each workspace. Returning starts new stores from the
			page's server values. SSR and tRPC call the same server function, backed by
			a typed SQL query.
		</p>
		<a class="back" href="/">Back to drafts →</a>
	</section>
</Page>
